1
00:00:08,038 --> 00:00:11,858
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

2
00:00:12,725 --> 00:00:14,084
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

3
00:00:14,317 --> 00:00:29,839
إِنَّ اللّهَ اصْطَفى آدَمَ وَ نُوحاً وَ آلَ إِبْراهیمَ وَ آلَ عِمْرانَ عَلَى الْعالَمینَ۝

4
00:00:30,579 --> 00:00:42,445
ذُرِّيَّةًۢ بَعْضُهَا مِنۢ بَعْضٍۢ ۗ وَٱللَّهُ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٌ۝

5
00:00:43,225 --> 00:00:52,475
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; Allah chose Adam(آدَم), Nuh(نوح), the family of Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم), and the family of Imran(عمران) above Al-Alameen(الْعالَمینَ).

6
00:00:52,728 --> 00:00:56,568
Offspring one of the other and Allah is All Hearer, All Knower.

7
00:00:56,855 --> 00:00:59,411
Adam(آدَم) was chosen; Istafa(اصْطَفى);

8
00:00:59,484 --> 00:01:01,351
 Istafa(اصْطَفى) means; chose.

9
00:01:02,091 --> 00:01:06,690
So Adam(آدَم) is chosen and Nuh(نوح).

10
00:01:07,423 --> 00:01:09,103
And then, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

11
00:01:09,156 --> 00:01:10,170
 آلَ إِبْراهیمَ

12
00:01:10,196 --> 00:01:10,403
And;

13
00:01:10,423 --> 00:01:11,410
آلَ عِمْرانَ

14
00:01:11,996 --> 00:01:14,909
With Adam(آدَم) and Nuh(نوح); Allahسُبحانه وتعالى mentioned their names alone;

15
00:01:14,989 --> 00:01:15,865
Adam(آدَم) and Nuh(نوح).

16
00:01:15,889 --> 00:01:17,763
إِنَّ اللّهَ اصْطَفى آدَمَ وَ نُوحاً

17
00:01:18,196 --> 00:01:20,057
Allah has chosen Adam(آدَم) and Nuh(نوح).

18
00:01:20,477 --> 00:01:25,100
But with Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) and Imran(عمران), Allah said; Aal-Ibrahim(آل-اِبْراهِيْم) and Aal-Imran(آل-عمران).

19
00:01:25,140 --> 00:01:26,453
And Aal(آل) means; the family.

20
00:01:26,646 --> 00:01:36,432
So, Adam(آدَم) was chosen; Nuh(نوح) was chosen, and then, Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) and his family were chosen, and Imran(عمران) and his family were chosen.

21
00:01:36,998 --> 00:01:38,357
ذُرِّيَّةًۢ بَعْضُهَا مِنۢ بَعْضٍۢ ۗ

22
00:01:38,384 --> 00:01:43,277
They are offspring of one another because; Aal-Imran(ال-عمران) are from the descendants of Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم),

23
00:01:43,463 --> 00:01:48,401
and Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) is from the descendants of Nuh(نوح), and Nuh(نوح) is from the descendants of Adam(آدَم).

24
00:01:48,568 --> 00:01:51,075
These are the chosen ones of the world.

25
00:01:51,648 --> 00:01:59,524
But then the chosen out of all humanity and all of the creation is; Muhammadﷺ.

26
00:01:59,911 --> 00:02:05,807
Aal-Ibrahim(آل-اِبْراهِيْم) and Aal-Imran(آل-عمران); and Aal-Ibrahim(آل-اِبْراهِيْم) includes the ones who believe in the message of truth.

27
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:09,579
Because, we know that part of the family of Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) are Al-Yahood(اليهود).

28
00:02:09,872 --> 00:02:17,717
But they are not included in this; because as soon as there is Kuffr(كفر), then the ties of relationship are cut.

29
00:02:18,490 --> 00:02:21,257
So they are not part of the Aal-Ibrahim(آل-اِبْراهِيْم) anymore.

30
00:02:21,757 --> 00:02:26,433
And that's why, Ahl al-Bayt(اهل البيت) does not include within them; Abu Lahab(ابو لهب);

31
00:02:26,906 --> 00:02:28,950
Abu Lahab(ابو لهب) is not considered from Ahl al-Bayt(اهل البيت);

32
00:02:29,910 --> 00:02:33,783
Ahl al-Bayt(اهل البيت) of Rasool Allah ﷺ are the ones who believed in Muhammadﷺ from his family.

33
00:02:34,043 --> 00:02:36,635
But the ones who did not believe, they're not included in Ahl al-Bayt(اهل البيت).

34
00:02:37,128 --> 00:02:39,475
And the same thing with Nuh(نوح) when he said; This is my son,

35
00:02:39,688 --> 00:02:44,847
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told him; He's not from your family, he is not part of your relatives to start with.

36
00:02:45,167 --> 00:02:46,347
إِنَّهُۥ عَمَلٌ غَيْرُ صَٰلِحٍۢ ۖ

37
00:02:46,380 --> 00:02:48,043
Because, he's on unrighteous deeds.

38
00:02:48,883 --> 00:02:54,551
Aal-Imran(آل-عمران) are from the descendants of Sayidina Ibrahimعليه السلام.

39
00:02:55,491 --> 00:03:05,391
And Aal-Imran(آل-عمران) are the family of Sayidina Eesaعليه السلام, and that's the family of Zakariyya عليه السلام, and the family of Yahya عليه السلام.

40
00:03:05,438 --> 00:03:07,958
They are from the family the household of Aal-Imran(آل-عمران).

41
00:03:08,651 --> 00:03:09,707
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

42
00:03:09,747 --> 00:03:15,207
إِذْ قَالَتِ امْرَأَتُ عِمْرَانَ رَبِّ إِنِّي نَذَرْتُ لَكَ مَا فِي بَطْنِي

43
00:03:15,447 --> 00:03:21,740
This righteous woman; the wife of Imran(عمران); Imran(عمران) is the name of the father.

44
00:03:21,773 --> 00:03:24,027
He's the head of this household; his name is Imran(عمران).

45
00:03:24,987 --> 00:03:31,766
His wife said; Oh Allah! I vowed to you; what is in my womb.

46
00:03:32,533 --> 00:03:34,219
نَذَرْتُ لَكَ مَا فِي بَطْنِي

47
00:03:34,453 --> 00:03:37,619
An-Nazr(نَذَرْ) is a promise and a vow that you give.

48
00:03:38,279 --> 00:03:44,390
Imra'tu Imran(امرأة عمران); she gave a vow; a promise that, what is in a womb(she was pregnant) is for Allah.

49
00:03:44,823 --> 00:03:49,656
Specifically, that means that, this child will serve in the Masjid(مسجد).

50
00:03:50,509 --> 00:03:51,376
Which Masjid(مسجد)?

51
00:03:52,003 --> 00:03:52,976
Al-Masjid al-Aqsa(المسجد الاقصى).

52
00:03:53,356 --> 00:03:58,516
In that time they used to have men, who are devoted to Khidmat ul Masjid(خدمت المسجد).

53
00:03:58,983 --> 00:04:02,029
They were devoted to the serving of the Masjid(مسجد).

54
00:04:03,169 --> 00:04:07,258
The ones, who would fill this job were men.

55
00:04:07,465 --> 00:04:12,412
They didn't allow a women to take this job; it was for men.

56
00:04:13,012 --> 00:04:17,064
And they would live their entire life in the Masjid(مسجد) and serve in the Masjid(مسجد).

57
00:04:18,284 --> 00:04:23,676
So Imra'tu Imran(امرأة عمران) said; Oh Allah! I'm vowing my child to you; to the Khidmah(خدمة) of Al-Masjid(المسجد).

58
00:04:23,896 --> 00:04:30,078
And I think these Ayaat(آيات); that deals with the parents and children; we need to reflect on them.

59
00:04:30,404 --> 00:04:33,227
We're not going to spend a lot of time doing this reflection now.

60
00:04:33,567 --> 00:04:37,313
But take this as a pointer and a tip, when you're reading through the Ayaat(آيات) of Qur'an,

61
00:04:37,546 --> 00:04:45,112
when you see the relations between the parents and the children within the righteous families; try to think about it and reflect and contemplate.

62
00:04:45,285 --> 00:04:50,297
Over here, Imra'tu Imran(امرأة عمران) is vowing her child to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى to serve in the Masjid(مسجد).

63
00:04:51,351 --> 00:04:54,456
Imra'tu Imran(امرأة عمران); she was not thinking in terms of Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) at all.

64
00:04:55,116 --> 00:04:59,789
She wanted her child to go to the service in the Masjid al-Aqsa(مسجد الاقصى).

65
00:05:00,863 --> 00:05:05,381
Not for a certain time, and then come back to her and generate money; For the whole life.

66
00:05:06,208 --> 00:05:10,450
She wants her son because the service is for men.

67
00:05:10,704 --> 00:05:13,650
She wanted her son to go in the Masjid(مسجد) and serve in the Masjid(مسجد).

68
00:05:14,250 --> 00:05:18,607
I think; we should learn from the ones, whom Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has chosen.

69
00:05:18,627 --> 00:05:21,874
These are the ones whom Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given Istafa(اصْطَفى).

70
00:05:22,161 --> 00:05:24,050
And they should be the role models for us.

71
00:05:24,803 --> 00:05:31,477
We need to take care of the religious matters of our children more than the Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) matters.

72
00:05:31,517 --> 00:05:33,977
Because the one, who is giving them Rizq(رزق) is Allah not us.

73
00:05:34,804 --> 00:05:36,570
We are not the ones, who are giving them Rizq(رزق).

74
00:05:36,923 --> 00:05:38,410
And that's why, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

75
00:05:38,430 --> 00:05:40,456
نَّحْنُ نَرْزُقُهُمْ وَإِيَّاكُمْ ۚ

76
00:05:40,616 --> 00:05:41,776
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

77
00:05:41,990 --> 00:05:44,638
نَحْنُ نَرْزُقُكُمْ وَإِيَّاهُمْ۝

78
00:05:44,678 --> 00:05:45,358
In two Ayaat(آيات).

79
00:05:45,585 --> 00:05:49,227
One Ayah(آية), Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; We give you Rizq(رزق), and We give them Rizq(رزق).

80
00:05:49,300 --> 00:05:51,854
And in another Ayah(آية), Allah says; We give them Rizq(رزق), and We give you Rizq(رزق).

81
00:05:52,100 --> 00:05:55,174
One time; they will mentioned before us, and one time we were mentioned before them.

82
00:05:55,774 --> 00:05:58,286
In all; Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is the One, Who is giving Rizq(رزق).

83
00:05:58,666 --> 00:06:04,278
Allah is the One, Who created every human being, and Allahسُبحانه وتعالى created with the human being its Rizq(رزق).

84
00:06:04,771 --> 00:06:06,338
We are not the ones, who are providing for them.

85
00:06:06,705 --> 00:06:11,609
Therefore, we need to pay attention to the religious matters of our children.

86
00:06:11,742 --> 00:06:13,029
And that's why, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

87
00:06:13,096 --> 00:06:16,548
قُوا أَنفُسَكُمْ وَأَهْلِيكُمْ نَارًا وَقُودُهَا النَّاسُ وَالْحِجَارَةُ

88
00:06:16,695 --> 00:06:22,707
Save yourselves and your families from hell fire. Save yourselves and your families from Hellfire.

89
00:06:24,007 --> 00:06:26,473
Now, He didn't say; save themselves from hunger even though; we should.

90
00:06:27,053 --> 00:06:33,320
So Imra'tu Imran(امرأة عمران) was devoting her child to the serving of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى in Al-Masjid al-Aqsa(المسجد الاقصى).

91
00:06:33,500 --> 00:06:34,049
And then, she said;

92
00:06:34,074 --> 00:06:35,055
مُحَرَّرًا

93
00:06:35,449 --> 00:06:38,122
نَذَرْتُ لَكَ مَا فِي بَطْنِي مُحَرَّرًا

94
00:06:38,462 --> 00:06:40,755
Free from all worldly work.

95
00:06:41,735 --> 00:06:45,798
If we just take the word Muharrar(مُحَرَّر), it means; free; freedom.

96
00:06:46,038 --> 00:06:51,964
This word freedom has been used by every revolutionary group in the world.

97
00:06:52,078 --> 00:06:55,351
Everyone is seeking freedom.

98
00:06:56,338 --> 00:07:01,240
Every movement of revolution comes under the banner of freedom.

99
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:07,020
Freedom is a quality that every human being is striving to get.

100
00:07:07,686 --> 00:07:13,621
And over here, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is giving us the definition of this Istalah(اصطلاح); the definition of this word.

101
00:07:13,975 --> 00:07:15,115
What is freedom?

102
00:07:15,535 --> 00:07:16,695
Because we all want freedom.

103
00:07:17,051 --> 00:07:18,751
So what's the meaning of this word?

104
00:07:19,264 --> 00:07:21,384
What's the definition of freedom?

105
00:07:21,771 --> 00:07:26,123
And we get the definition from the mouth of the wife of Imran(عمران).

106
00:07:27,983 --> 00:07:35,608
When she said that, her child is going to be the servant of Allah, in the Masjid(مسجد) of Allah.

107
00:07:36,288 --> 00:07:43,228
When her son is going into servitude; Abudiyyah(عبوديه); to serve Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

108
00:07:43,428 --> 00:07:47,081
She said; that is Tehreer(تحرير); that is the freedom for my child.

109
00:07:47,287 --> 00:07:52,190
Because if you are not a slave of Allah; you're going to be a slave of something else.

110
00:07:53,423 --> 00:07:57,110
If you're not a servant of Allah; you're going to be serve something else.

111
00:07:57,710 --> 00:08:08,174
If you don't serve Allah; you're going to serve money, you're going to serve your desires, you might serve a king, or a human being.

112
00:08:08,708 --> 00:08:17,379
The only way that you could be free and is when; you devote yourself in sincerity and you serve Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

113
00:08:17,619 --> 00:08:18,806
That's the only way you could be free.

114
00:08:19,239 --> 00:08:24,091
And that's why, Rabie Bin Aamir(ربيع بن عامر); when he went to meet with the Persian commander,

115
00:08:25,771 --> 00:08:28,024
and the Persian commander said; What did you come here for?

116
00:08:28,758 --> 00:08:32,816
Because the Persian commander knows the Arab people before Islam.

117
00:08:33,163 --> 00:08:44,153
The Arab people before Islam were dis-united tribes, hungry, poor; and they were so poor; they would eat the skin of dead animals.

118
00:08:44,853 --> 00:08:47,635
They would eat dead animals; but they would also sometimes eat the skin.

119
00:08:47,835 --> 00:08:56,476
And that was the stereotype that the Persians had; the Persian Empire had about the Arabs of Arabia.

120
00:08:56,516 --> 00:08:57,683
تأکلون جلود الميته

121
00:08:57,716 --> 00:09:02,405
You are so poor that you eat the skin of dead animals.

122
00:09:02,659 --> 00:09:04,465
What are you doing here in the Persian Empire?

123
00:09:04,579 --> 00:09:07,187
This is too advanced for you to come in, what are you doing here?

124
00:09:07,787 --> 00:09:13,816
And then he told him; if you came here because, you need money; I'll give every one of you a certain amount of money.

125
00:09:13,929 --> 00:09:16,289
And then I will give your Ameer(أمير) double.

126
00:09:16,843 --> 00:09:17,916
Go back to your land!

127
00:09:18,376 --> 00:09:19,889
Rabie Bin Aamir(ربيع بن عامر) said;

128
00:09:19,996 --> 00:09:27,778
ابتعثنا الله لنخرج العبادمن عبادة العباد إلى عبادة رب العبادمن عبادة العباد إلى عبادة رب العبادومن ضيق الدنيا إلى سَعَتِ الدُّنيَا وَلآخِرَة

129
00:09:28,224 --> 00:09:30,444
ومن جور الأديان الی سعت الإسلام

130
00:09:31,258 --> 00:09:31,511
He said;

131
00:09:31,531 --> 00:09:42,885
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has sent us, so that we can deliver the creation of Allah, from being slaves of each other, to being the slaves of Allah,

132
00:09:44,185 --> 00:09:50,648
and from the narrowness of this world, to the vastness of this world and the Hereafter,

133
00:09:51,695 --> 00:09:56,263
and from the oppression of other religions to the justice of Islam.

134
00:09:56,883 --> 00:10:02,476
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى sent us to free you, from serving each other, to serving Allah.

135
00:10:03,296 --> 00:10:07,242
Because, you are not serving Allah therefore, you're serving each other.

136
00:10:07,642 --> 00:10:09,661
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى sent us to free you from this.

137
00:10:09,701 --> 00:10:12,875
So that, you could serve Allahسُبحانه وتعالى and stop serving one another.

138
00:10:13,821 --> 00:10:18,380
And this is the message of Islam; to free the human being; So that the human being can be;

139
00:10:18,900 --> 00:10:20,794
مخلصاً بالله عزّوجل

140
00:10:21,140 --> 00:10:22,854
Pure for Allahسُبحانه وتعالى;

141
00:10:23,860 --> 00:10:24,813
فَتَقَبَّلْ مِنِّىٓ ۖ

142
00:10:24,846 --> 00:10:26,426
Oh Allah! Accept for me;

143
00:10:26,640 --> 00:10:28,486
إِنَّكَ أَنتَ ٱلسَّمِيعُ ٱلْعَلِيمُ۝

144
00:10:28,553 --> 00:10:33,173
Oh Allah! You are verily the All hearer and the All knowerer.

145
00:10:33,613 --> 00:10:52,470
فَلَمَّا وَضَعَتْهَا قَالَتْ رَبِّ إِنِّي وَضَعْتُهَا أُنثَىٰ وَاللَّهُ أَعْلَمُ بِمَا وَضَعَتْ وَلَيْسَ الذَّكَرُ كَالْأُنثَىٰ ۖ

146
00:10:52,956 --> 00:11:00,956
When she delivered her child, she said; Oh my Lord! I have given birth to a female child.

147
00:11:01,138 --> 00:11:04,551
Imra'tu Imran(امرأة عمران); she had a female child.

148
00:11:05,697 --> 00:11:13,980
And females were not traditionally allowed to serve in the Masjid(مسجد); it was only for men.

149
00:11:15,060 --> 00:11:18,887
So she said; Oh Allah! I delivered a female.

150
00:11:19,354 --> 00:11:20,441
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

151
00:11:20,461 --> 00:11:22,241
وَاللَّهُ أَعْلَمُ بِمَا وَضَعَتْ

152
00:11:22,281 --> 00:11:25,041
Allah knows better; what she delivered.

153
00:11:26,014 --> 00:11:27,374
And then, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

154
00:11:27,394 --> 00:11:29,556
وَلَيْسَ الذَّكَرُ كَالْأُنثَىٰ ۖ

155
00:11:30,043 --> 00:11:33,383
And the male is not like the female.

156
00:11:34,023 --> 00:11:34,936
What does this mean?

157
00:11:35,763 --> 00:11:37,356
وَلَيْسَ الذَّكَرُ كَالْأُنثَىٰ ۖ

158
00:11:38,323 --> 00:11:43,271
Imra'tu Imran(امرأة عمران); she wanted to have a son; a male; so the male could serve in the Masjid(مسجد).

159
00:11:44,591 --> 00:11:49,004
When she was not given a son and was given a daughter; she was upset.

160
00:11:49,218 --> 00:11:53,277
And then, she said; Oh Allahسُبحانه وتعالى! I have delivered a female.

161
00:11:54,377 --> 00:11:59,638
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; Allah knows best is what you delivered, and the male is not like the female.

162
00:12:00,665 --> 00:12:07,471
This means that, whatever male you would have delivered; that male will not be better than the female that Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given you.

163
00:12:07,811 --> 00:12:12,157
Because the female that Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given you is the best of Nisa al-Alameen(نساءلعالمين).

164
00:12:13,997 --> 00:12:14,984
She doesn't know;

165
00:12:15,097 --> 00:12:16,419
اَللَّهُ أَعْلَمُ بِمَا وَضَعَتْ

166
00:12:16,485 --> 00:12:17,365
Allah knows better.

167
00:12:17,472 --> 00:12:21,605
All what she knows; Imra'tu Imran(امرأة عمران); all what she knows is that; she delivered a female. But;

168
00:12:21,625 --> 00:12:22,981
اَللَّهُ أَعْلَمُ بِمَا وَضَعَتْ

169
00:12:23,001 --> 00:12:25,763
Allah knows; who this female is.?

170
00:12:25,937 --> 00:12:27,843
And this female is; Maryamعليها السلام.

171
00:12:28,883 --> 00:12:30,090
اَللَّهُ أَعْلَمُ بِمَا وَضَعَتْ

172
00:12:30,117 --> 00:12:32,089
Allah knows best; what she delivered.

173
00:12:32,296 --> 00:12:33,742
وَلَيْسَ الذَّكَرُ كَالْأُنثَىٰ ۖ

174
00:12:33,762 --> 00:12:35,396
The male will never be like the female.

175
00:12:35,742 --> 00:12:38,591
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Has given you a blessing.

176
00:12:38,611 --> 00:12:44,300
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given you the best woman that will ever live on the face of the earth and that is; Sayidatna Maryam(سيدتنا مريم).

177
00:12:44,320 --> 00:12:45,366
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

178
00:12:45,406 --> 00:12:46,793
خيرُ نساءِ العالمينَ أربعٌ

179
00:12:46,946 --> 00:12:48,795
The best of the woman of the world are four;

180
00:12:49,002 --> 00:12:53,442
Maryam(مريم) and Asiyah(آسيه) and Khadijah(خديجه) and Fatimah binte Muhammad(فاطمه بنتِ محمدﷺ).

181
00:12:53,562 --> 00:12:54,691
These are the best four.

182
00:12:55,198 --> 00:12:59,398
And the best of them all; was Maryam Binte Imranعليها السلام.

183
00:13:01,378 --> 00:13:08,240
وَاللَّهُ أَعْلَمُ بِمَا وَضَعَتْ وَلَيْسَ الذَّكَرُ كَالْأُنثَىٰ ۖ وَإِنِّي سَمَّيْتُهَا مَرْيَمَ

184
00:13:08,300 --> 00:13:10,224
She named the child Maryam(مريم).

185
00:13:10,718 --> 00:13:13,424
That's the name she chose for the child; Maryam(مريم).

186
00:13:13,771 --> 00:13:21,280
Rasool Allah ﷺ says; every child who is born is stabbed by Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ).

187
00:13:22,740 --> 00:13:27,043
Whenever a child is born, what's the first thing that the child does?

188
00:13:28,030 --> 00:13:29,130
When the child is born?

189
00:13:29,476 --> 00:13:30,050
Cry?

190
00:13:30,676 --> 00:13:32,147
The first thing they do; they cry.

191
00:13:32,401 --> 00:13:32,901
They come out;

192
00:13:32,927 --> 00:13:34,137
یستحل صالحٓا

193
00:13:34,354 --> 00:13:35,587
They come out; crying.

194
00:13:35,661 --> 00:13:36,502
Why do they cry?

195
00:13:37,202 --> 00:13:46,791
Rasool Allah ﷺ says in this Hadith(حديث) is a Muslim that; Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) stabs every child and that's why, the child comes out crying.

196
00:13:49,178 --> 00:13:57,207
And by the way, before continuing the Hadith(حديث); you can see how much Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) hates human beings.

197
00:13:58,287 --> 00:14:01,307
From the moment you're born, he stabs you.

198
00:14:01,681 --> 00:14:03,567
As soon as you come out; he stabs you.

199
00:14:03,827 --> 00:14:06,973
He hates humanity so much.

200
00:14:07,767 --> 00:14:12,385
Subhan Allah(سُبْحان الله)! Who would like to harm, who would want to harm such a lovely child.

201
00:14:13,052 --> 00:14:18,375
But this shows you the evilness and the wickedness of Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ).

202
00:14:18,828 --> 00:14:22,635
And it shows you; how foolish humans are when they follow Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ).

203
00:14:23,181 --> 00:14:25,714
الشَّيْطَانَ لَكُمْ عَدُوٌّ فَاتَّخِذُوهُ عَدُوًّا ۚ

204
00:14:25,747 --> 00:14:27,647
Like Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) and Adam(آدَم) has given us advice.

205
00:14:27,667 --> 00:14:28,294
He said;

206
00:14:28,760 --> 00:14:31,348
If Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) is your enemy, so take him as an enemy.

207
00:14:32,415 --> 00:14:35,960
He's our enemy; from day one he is our enemy, and we should take him as our enemy.

208
00:14:37,060 --> 00:14:38,684
وَكَانَ ٱلشَّيْطَٰنُ لِلْإِنسَٰنِ خَذُولًا۝

209
00:14:38,710 --> 00:14:41,479
he is betraying the son of Adam(آدَم).

210
00:14:42,186 --> 00:14:43,913
This happens to every child.

211
00:14:44,746 --> 00:14:46,758
There is an exception of two.

212
00:14:47,484 --> 00:14:48,111
Who are they?

213
00:14:48,478 --> 00:14:51,558
Who are the who are not stabbed by Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ)?

214
00:14:52,811 --> 00:14:53,700
Maryam(مريم) and Eesa(عيسى).

215
00:14:54,026 --> 00:14:55,493
Maryam(مريم) and Eesa(عيسى) are the only exceptions.

216
00:14:55,666 --> 00:15:05,158
Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) has stabbed every child that was born, with the exception of Maryam(مريم) and Eesa(عيسى); Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) did not stab them.

217
00:15:05,238 --> 00:15:06,032
Why?

218
00:15:06,778 --> 00:15:10,117
Because of the Dua(دُعَا) of the mother of Maryam(مريم).

219
00:15:10,410 --> 00:15:14,483
وَإِنِّي أُعِيذُهَا بِكَ وَذُرِّيَّتَهَا مِنَ الشَّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيمِ۝

220
00:15:14,696 --> 00:15:20,975
And I seek refuge with You Allah, for her and for her offspring from Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ).

221
00:15:21,835 --> 00:15:29,640
So the mother said; Oh Allah! I seek refuge in You to save my child and her offspring from Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ).

222
00:15:30,840 --> 00:15:33,247
So child is Maryam(مريم), and who's the offspring of Maryam(مريم)?

223
00:15:33,707 --> 00:15:36,337
Eesa(عيسى), and its stop right there, there was no other offspring.

224
00:15:36,685 --> 00:15:40,838
So these are the only two, who were excluded from this stabbing of Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ).

225
00:15:41,105 --> 00:15:44,430
Rasool Allah ﷺ says; When he wanted to stab Eesa(عيسى);

226
00:15:44,650 --> 00:15:45,797
زھب یتعن فی الحجاب

227
00:15:45,822 --> 00:15:48,609
Al-Hijab(الحجاب) is the diaphragm; That's Al-Hijab(الحجاب).

228
00:15:48,955 --> 00:15:53,808
So, Eesaعليه السلام and Maryam(مريم) were saved from this stabbing of Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ).

229
00:15:53,894 --> 00:15:57,981
By the way, even though, Christianity claims to be the religion of Eesa(عيسى).

230
00:15:58,354 --> 00:16:01,880
They are missing many of the details of the life of Eesa(عيسى) to start with.

231
00:16:03,366 --> 00:16:05,722
And this is one thing that is missing.

232
00:16:06,842 --> 00:16:11,695
The issue, that Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has saved Maryam(مريم) and Eesa(عيسى) in their birth.

233
00:16:12,069 --> 00:16:19,758
And another thing that is missing, and it's one of the best or the most wonderful miracles that Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Has given Sayidina Eesa(سيدنا عيسى) is;

234
00:16:19,931 --> 00:16:20,938
يتكلم في المهد

235
00:16:21,224 --> 00:16:22,773
Speaking at birth.

236
00:16:23,320 --> 00:16:24,653
This is not mentioned in the Bible.

237
00:16:25,233 --> 00:16:33,146
And this is a knowledge that the people who claim to follow Eesa(عيسى), don't even know that Eesa(عيسى) spoke when he was born.

238
00:16:34,259 --> 00:16:37,578
And these are some of the miracles of Eesa(عيسى) that were mentioned in Qur'an.

239
00:16:39,004 --> 00:16:40,564
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

240
00:16:40,851 --> 00:16:45,640
فَتَقَبَّلَهَا رَبُّهَا بِقَبُولٍ حَسَنٍ وَأَنبَتَهَا نَبَاتًا حَسَنًا

241
00:16:46,633 --> 00:16:54,255
So her Lord accepted her with goodly acceptance; He made her grow in a good manner.

242
00:16:55,382 --> 00:17:01,604
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is the One, Who is growing up Maryam(مريم) in a Very good way.

243
00:17:02,211 --> 00:17:04,977
And this is a proof and an evidence

244
00:17:05,363 --> 00:17:15,426
that Maryam(مريم) since her birth, until the end of her life, was always righteous, was always taken care of by Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, and was always on the straight path.

245
00:17:16,446 --> 00:17:19,139
This is Sayidatna Maryam(سيدتنا مريم); Mary.

246
00:17:19,472 --> 00:17:23,984
And it's very important to note the fact that throughout her life;

247
00:17:24,697 --> 00:17:29,043
Why? Because the Jews accused Maryam(مريم).

248
00:17:29,996 --> 00:17:31,503
They accused her of Zina(زنا).

249
00:17:31,863 --> 00:17:34,243
They accused her of fornication.

250
00:17:35,476 --> 00:17:42,318
And they do not see Eesa(عيسى) as being a legitimate child.

251
00:17:42,785 --> 00:17:48,550
And they accuse her of sleeping with a carpenter and all of these made up fabricated stories.

252
00:17:49,264 --> 00:17:56,946
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is saying the contrary that; Maryam(مريم); Mary, since her birth until the end of her life, was always As-Siddiqah(الصّدّيقه).

253
00:17:57,386 --> 00:17:59,625
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى always called her As-Siddiqah(الصّدّيقه) Qur'an.

254
00:17:59,652 --> 00:18:08,764
As-Siddiqah(الصّدّيقه) is an extreme form of righteousness, or it's a high level of righteousness due to an extreme form Sadaq(صدق); truth.

255
00:18:09,870 --> 00:18:19,265
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى in many Ayaat(آيات) and Rasool Allah ﷺ in many Ahadith(احاديث) told us about the virtues of Sadaq(صدق); truth.

256
00:18:19,865 --> 00:18:24,820
Rasool Allah ﷺ says that Sadaq(صدق); truth leads to righteousness, and righteousness leads to paradise.

257
00:18:25,233 --> 00:18:32,396
And the man would continue saying the truth until, he is written by Allahسُبحانه وتعالى as being As-Siddique(الصّدّيق).

258
00:18:32,809 --> 00:18:40,106
The more truth you say, and the more truthful you are; the closer you are to the status; the station of Siddique(صدّيق).

259
00:18:40,913 --> 00:18:47,069
And the best or the most prominent type of truth is being truthful with Allah.

260
00:18:48,135 --> 00:18:54,481
There's different forms of truth; truth with the creation, truth with yourself and then, there's truth with Allah.

261
00:18:54,941 --> 00:18:57,851
The highest of all; is the truth with Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

262
00:18:58,778 --> 00:19:02,550
And you are true with your covenant to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

263
00:19:02,570 --> 00:19:03,503
What does that mean?

264
00:19:04,410 --> 00:19:06,158
When you say that you are a Muslim;

265
00:19:06,752 --> 00:19:14,361
truth with Allah means that you are true in that claim, and you fulfill all of the terms of the contract between you and Allah.

266
00:19:14,427 --> 00:19:17,181
Because, we have a contract between us and Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

267
00:19:18,867 --> 00:19:20,293
And that's the highest level of truth.

268
00:19:20,333 --> 00:19:23,167
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى said about the Sahabah(صحابه) that; They are men;

269
00:19:23,380 --> 00:19:24,727
صَدَقُوا مَا عَاهَدُوا اللَّهَ عَلَيْهِ ۖ

270
00:19:24,767 --> 00:19:27,931
They have been truthful, in their covenant with Allah.

271
00:19:28,264 --> 00:19:29,264
They gave Allah Bay'ah(بيعه).

272
00:19:29,604 --> 00:19:30,864
صَدَقُوا مَا عَاهَدُوا اللَّهَ عَلَيْهِ ۖ

273
00:19:30,884 --> 00:19:34,360
Ahd(عهد) is a contract or Ahd(عهد) is a promise between you and Allah.

274
00:19:34,660 --> 00:19:40,309
Sahabah(صحابه) gave Allah a promise; they have a contract between them and Allah.

275
00:19:40,809 --> 00:19:46,868
And that contract is that; they are going to worship nobody but Allah, and that; they are going to give Nusrah(نصرة); victory to the religion of Allah.

276
00:19:47,195 --> 00:19:49,541
And they have fulfilled the terms of that contract.

277
00:19:49,601 --> 00:19:56,446
So, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says about them; They are men whom fulfilled and have been truthful with Allah.

278
00:19:57,059 --> 00:19:58,293
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

279
00:19:58,533 --> 00:19:59,789
وَأُمُّهُۥ صِدِّيقَةٌ ۖ

280
00:19:59,889 --> 00:20:02,258
When Allah was talking about Sayidina Eesa(سيدنا عيسى); Jesus, Allah said;

281
00:20:02,312 --> 00:20:04,418
And his mother was As-Siddiqah(الصّدّيقة).

282
00:20:04,698 --> 00:20:10,067
So, she have reached this level, and what is the next level above Siddique(صدّيق)?

283
00:20:10,940 --> 00:20:13,374
Nabi(نَبِي); that's the highest, it could get.

284
00:20:13,614 --> 00:20:15,469
And then after that you get into Prophet-hood.

285
00:20:16,509 --> 00:20:19,323
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

286
00:20:19,789 --> 00:20:21,276
وَكَفَّلَهَا زَكَرِيَّا ۖ

287
00:20:21,856 --> 00:20:25,723
She was taken care of by Zakariyya(زَكَرِيا); Zachariah.

288
00:20:25,873 --> 00:20:30,767
Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) says that; Jumhurul-Ulama(جمهُوْرُالْعُلَمَا); the majority of the scholars say that,

289
00:20:31,047 --> 00:20:34,252
Maryam(مريم) is the sister in law of the Zakariyya(زَكَرِيا).

290
00:20:35,852 --> 00:20:40,985
So the wife of Zakariyya(زَكَرِيا); her name is Eeshia(عيشیا) and Maryam(مريم) is her sister.

291
00:20:42,058 --> 00:20:47,751
Some other scholars say that; she's her nice.

292
00:20:48,837 --> 00:20:53,907
Because, they say that Eeshia(عيشیا); actually is the sister of the mother of Maryam(مريم).

293
00:20:54,194 --> 00:20:59,409
So there's a bit of a difference of opinion here, but it's an irrelevant difference of opinion.

294
00:21:00,942 --> 00:21:03,035
But we know that they are relatives.

295
00:21:03,955 --> 00:21:06,204
Zakariyya(زَكَرِيا) is the one, who took care of her.

296
00:21:06,417 --> 00:21:11,312
The way this happened; and just to refresh your memory again that;

297
00:21:11,845 --> 00:21:15,072
Imra'tu Imran(امرأة عمران); the mother of Maryam(مريم), she said;

298
00:21:15,498 --> 00:21:21,171
I'm giving whatever I'm going to deliver to the service of Al-Masjid(المسجد).

299
00:21:21,924 --> 00:21:25,789
The Jews had this law or tradition that,

300
00:21:25,843 --> 00:21:36,211
they would devote some men entirely and completely to take care of Al-Masjid(المسجد) to service the Masjid(مسجد); Al-Masjid Al-Aqsa(المسجد الاقصى).

301
00:21:36,998 --> 00:21:38,686
And this role was for men.

302
00:21:40,066 --> 00:21:43,879
But they accepted Maryam(مريم) even though, she was a woman.

303
00:21:44,959 --> 00:21:51,361
When she was very young, her mother handed her over to the care keepers of Al-Masjid(المسجد),

304
00:21:52,601 --> 00:21:55,133
because she came from this noble and blessed family.

305
00:21:55,173 --> 00:21:59,766
And by the way, the family of Al-Imran(آل-عمران) are the descendants of Dawoodعليه السلام.

306
00:22:01,873 --> 00:22:05,311
Because she is from this blessed family and Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

307
00:22:05,331 --> 00:22:10,173
إِنَّ اللّهَ اصْطَفى آدَمَ وَ نُوحاً وَ آلَ إِبْراهیمَ وَ آلَ عِمْرانَ

308
00:22:10,687 --> 00:22:11,629
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

309
00:22:11,669 --> 00:22:20,101
We have chosen Adam(آدَم), and Nuh(نوح), and the family of Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم), and the family of Imran(عمران) over all, mankind.

310
00:22:21,028 --> 00:22:22,768
So this is a very blessed family.

311
00:22:23,994 --> 00:22:30,756
Due to the fact that, they are very blessed and noble family among their people; Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل); the children of Israel(اسرائيل);

312
00:22:31,330 --> 00:22:38,187
everyone wanted to take care of Maryam(مريم), everyone wanted that honour.

313
00:22:39,280 --> 00:22:46,776
So all of these men, who are the keepers of Al-Masjid al-Aqsa(المسجد الاقصى) are disputing among themselves,

314
00:22:46,810 --> 00:22:51,725
who would have the honour of taking care of Maryam(مريم) to raise her up.

315
00:22:51,759 --> 00:22:54,620
Because, you have to go through training, to take care of the Masjid(مسجد).

316
00:22:54,974 --> 00:23:04,016
So, they were competing and who would get the honour of having Maryam(مريم) so that, they could train her, for the position of being a caretaker of Al-Masjid(المسجد).

317
00:23:05,376 --> 00:23:08,900
They couldn't solve the dispute, so they ended up casting lots.

318
00:23:09,160 --> 00:23:10,633
They used to cast lots.

319
00:23:10,927 --> 00:23:14,000
And by the way, this is something that the nations before use to do.

320
00:23:14,613 --> 00:23:18,438
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Has replaced us with something better, and what does that?

321
00:23:19,438 --> 00:23:20,625
Salatu Istikhara(صلاة استخارا).

322
00:23:21,332 --> 00:23:23,745
The nations before, they didn't know about Salatu Istikhara(صلاة استخارا).

323
00:23:24,272 --> 00:23:27,053
This is something reserved for the ummah(امة) of Muhammadﷺ.

324
00:23:27,893 --> 00:23:29,420
So they had to cast lots.

325
00:23:29,700 --> 00:23:31,127
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

326
00:23:31,517 --> 00:23:40,996
ذَٰلِكَ مِنْ أَنبَاءِ الْغَيْبِ نُوحِيهِ إِلَيْكَ ۚ

327
00:23:41,685 --> 00:23:58,565
وَمَا كُنتَ لَدَيْهِمْ إِذْ يُلْقُونَ أَقْلَامَهُمْ أَيُّهُمْ يَكْفُلُ مَرْيَمَ وَمَا كُنتَ لَدَيْهِمْ إِذْ يَخْتَصِمُونَ۝

328
00:23:59,265 --> 00:24:00,565
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

329
00:24:00,765 --> 00:24:07,880
These are the news of the unseen, you were not with them; when they were casting lots, and who would take care of Maryam(مريم),

330
00:24:08,167 --> 00:24:10,179
and you were not with them; when they were disputing.

331
00:24:10,653 --> 00:24:16,925
So they cast lots, and Allahسُبحانه وتعالى made them, the lots come out on who?

332
