499
00:37:40,825 --> 00:37:43,333
He said; he wants an Ayah(آية), Ayah(آية) mean; sign.

500
00:37:43,740 --> 00:37:44,962
قَالَ رَبِّ ٱجْعَل لِّىٓ ءَايَةً ۚ

501
00:37:44,982 --> 00:37:46,702
Oh Allah! Give me a sign.

502
00:37:47,549 --> 00:37:48,976
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

503
00:37:49,456 --> 00:37:57,456
قَالَ آيَتُكَ أَلَّا تُكَلِّمَ النَّاسَ ثَلَاثَةَ أَيَّامٍ إِلَّا رَمْزًا ۗ

504
00:37:57,771 --> 00:38:00,092
He said; Oh my Lord! Make a sign for me.

505
00:38:00,172 --> 00:38:06,981
Allah said; Your sign is that, you shall not speak to mankind for three days, except with signals.

506
00:38:07,728 --> 00:38:13,139
The meaning of the sign is that; Sayidina Zakariyyahعليه السلام would not be able to speak except Dhikr(ذكر).

507
00:38:13,379 --> 00:38:16,099
And this phase would continue for three days.

508
00:38:17,039 --> 00:38:18,268
So he speaks fine.

509
00:38:19,215 --> 00:38:23,055
And then, suddenly for three days; he lost the ability to speak.

510
00:38:23,855 --> 00:38:26,959
And he was only able to make Dhikr(ذكر) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

511
00:38:28,146 --> 00:38:30,082
So, how can he communicate with people?

512
00:38:30,528 --> 00:38:33,077
He communicate with them by; signs.

513
00:38:33,284 --> 00:38:34,004
He would make signs.

514
00:38:34,044 --> 00:38:34,870
إِلَّا رَمْزًا ۗ

515
00:38:35,150 --> 00:38:37,137
Except through signs.

516
00:38:38,137 --> 00:38:40,639
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told him during these three days;

517
00:38:40,739 --> 00:38:44,599
وَاذْكُر رَّبَّكَ كَثِيرًا وَسَبِّحْ بِالْعَشِيِّ وَالْإِبْكَارِ۝

518
00:38:44,866 --> 00:38:50,665
And remember your Lord much, and glorify Him in the afternoon and in the morning.

519
00:38:50,865 --> 00:38:52,637
And these are the time of Adhkaar(اذكار).

520
00:38:52,870 --> 00:38:55,077
When do we make the Dhikr(ذكر) of As-Sabah(الصباح)?

521
00:38:55,470 --> 00:38:56,703
We make it after Fajr(فجر).

522
00:38:57,857 --> 00:39:00,611
And when do we make the Dhikr(ذكر) of nighttime?

523
00:39:00,724 --> 00:39:02,704
We do it after Asr(عصر).

524
00:39:03,491 --> 00:39:04,778
And this is in this Ayah(آية).

525
00:39:04,984 --> 00:39:08,167
وَاذْكُر رَّبَّكَ كَثِيرًا وَسَبِّحْ بِالْعَشِيِّ وَالْإِبْكَارِ۝

526
00:39:08,234 --> 00:39:11,767
Remember the name of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى in the morning and afternoon.

527
00:39:12,487 --> 00:39:14,723
These were the Ayaat(آيات) from Surat(سورت) Al-Imran(آلعمران).

528
00:39:14,743 --> 00:39:21,458
Let's read the Ayaat(آيات) which are talking about the same story from Surat(سورت) Maryam(مريم).

529
00:39:22,045 --> 00:39:23,431
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

530
00:39:23,798 --> 00:39:28,649
ذِكْرُ رَحْمَتِ رَبِّكَ عَبْدَهُ زَكَرِيَّا۝

531
00:39:28,896 --> 00:39:34,798
إِذْ نَادَىٰ رَبَّهُ نِدَاءً خَفِيًّا۝

532
00:39:35,224 --> 00:39:48,682
قَالَ رَبِّ إِنِّي وَهَنَ الْعَظْمُ مِنِّي وَاشْتَعَلَ الرَّأْسُ شَيْبًا وَلَمْ أَكُن بِدُعَائِكَ رَبِّ شَقِيًّا۝

533
00:39:49,276 --> 00:39:59,400
وَإِنِّي خِفْتُ الْمَوَالِيَ مِن وَرَائِي وَكَانَتِ امْرَأَتِي عَاقِرًا فَهَبْ

534
00:39:59,680 --> 00:40:03,872
فَهَبْ لِي مِن لَّدُنكَ وَلِيًّا۝

535
00:40:04,059 --> 00:40:06,944
Allahسُبحانه وتعال says about Sayidina Zakariyya(سيدنا زَكَرِيا).

536
00:40:07,097 --> 00:40:07,377
He said;

537
00:40:07,404 --> 00:40:09,761
My Lord! Indeed my bones have grown feeble.

538
00:40:09,814 --> 00:40:10,667
He's very old.

539
00:40:11,374 --> 00:40:17,795
And gray hair has spread on my head, and I have never been unblessed in my invocation to you.

540
00:40:17,875 --> 00:40:20,855
He said; Oh Allah! You always respond to my Dua(دُعَا).

541
00:40:21,208 --> 00:40:22,075
Zakariyya(زَكَرِيا) said;

542
00:40:22,195 --> 00:40:24,255
وَإِنِّي خِفْتُ الْمَوَالِيَ مِن وَرَائِي

543
00:40:24,495 --> 00:40:26,868
I verily fear my relatives after me.

544
00:40:27,128 --> 00:40:35,547
Zakariyya عليه السلام being the Nabi(نَبِي); he was the one responsible for the religious affairs of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

545
00:40:36,887 --> 00:40:43,605
Sayidina Zakariyya(سيدنا زَكَرِيا), when he became old; he was worried that there's no one qualified to take over after him.

546
00:40:45,705 --> 00:40:53,069
Therefore, he wanted to have a child that would be strong and capable to lead Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل),

547
00:40:53,289 --> 00:40:56,635
and to teach them, and to bring them back to the straight path.

548
00:40:57,668 --> 00:40:58,208
So he said;

549
00:40:58,241 --> 00:40:59,607
فَهَبْ لِي مِن لَّدُنكَ وَلِيًّا۝

550
00:40:59,627 --> 00:41:01,780
So give me from Yourself a heir.

551
00:41:01,987 --> 00:41:08,852
يَرِثُنِي وَيَرِثُ مِنْ آلِ يَعْقُوبَ ۖ وَاجْعَلْهُ رَبِّ رَضِيًّا۝

552
00:41:09,192 --> 00:41:12,788
Who shall inherit me and inherit the property of Yaqoob(يعقوب).

553
00:41:13,068 --> 00:41:15,001
What inheritance are we talking about here?

554
00:41:15,588 --> 00:41:16,628
What is the inheritance?

555
00:41:17,701 --> 00:41:18,602
It is Prophet-hood.

556
00:41:18,848 --> 00:41:19,762
It is not wealth.

557
00:41:20,115 --> 00:41:22,160
Because Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

558
00:41:22,180 --> 00:41:24,085
إنَّا مَعَاشِرَالْأَنْبِيَاءِ لَا نُورَثُ

559
00:41:24,592 --> 00:41:28,792
We; the prophets; we do not leave behind an inheritance.

560
00:41:29,752 --> 00:41:31,042
مَا تَرَكْنَاهُ صَدَقَة

561
00:41:31,256 --> 00:41:33,469
Whatever we leave behind is As-Sadaqah(الصّدقه); charity.

562
00:41:34,362 --> 00:41:39,377
So, here Zakariyya(زَكَرِيا) wants to inherit to his son, Prophet-hood.

563
00:41:40,231 --> 00:41:45,813
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى said; Oh Zakariyya(زَكَرِيا)! Verily, We give you the glad tidings of a son.

564
00:41:46,553 --> 00:41:49,210
اسْمُهُ يَحْيَىٰ لَمْ نَجْعَل لَّهُ مِن قَبْلُ سَمِيًّا۝

565
00:41:49,543 --> 00:41:51,281
Here, we have another attribute of Yahya(يحيى).

566
00:41:51,434 --> 00:41:55,387
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; We have given that name to none before him.

567
00:41:55,607 --> 00:42:03,960
His name is Yahya(يحيى); the first person to be named Yahya(يحيى) in the whole history of the world, was Sayidina Yahyaعليه السلام.

568
00:42:04,056 --> 00:42:09,725
This was a new name that was chosen for Sayidina Yahyaعليه السلام before he was delivered.

569
00:42:10,255 --> 00:42:13,491
And this name was given to him by Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

570
00:42:13,538 --> 00:42:18,218
The name; Yahya(يحيى) was not chosen by the Zakariyya(زَكَرِيا) or his wife.

571
00:42:18,498 --> 00:42:21,151
The name Yahya(يحيى) was chosen by Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

572
00:42:21,171 --> 00:42:22,784
Allah is the one who named him Yahya(يحيى).

573
00:42:23,691 --> 00:42:28,137
And he asked the same question; how can this happen when I'm old and my wife is barren?

574
00:42:28,337 --> 00:42:30,032
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says here;

575
00:42:30,266 --> 00:42:41,267
قَالَ كَذَٰلِكَ قَالَ رَبُّكَ هُوَ عَلَيَّ هَيِّنٌ وَقَدْ خَلَقْتُكَ مِن قَبْلُ وَلَمْ تَكُ شَيْئًا۝

576
00:42:41,727 --> 00:42:44,713
He said; Your Lord says; it is easy for me.

577
00:42:45,000 --> 00:42:48,497
Certainly, I have created you before, when you have been nothing.

578
00:42:48,924 --> 00:42:52,065
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى said; it's easy for me to create Yahya(يحيى) this way.

579
00:42:52,305 --> 00:42:53,645
You were nothing before.

580
00:42:54,159 --> 00:42:59,037
Just like, you were nothing; it's easy to create Yahya عليه السلام.

581
00:42:59,064 --> 00:43:08,279
Now, the following Ayaat(آيات), or actually, this Ayah(آية) is also similar to the Ayah(آية) of Al-Imran(آلعمران) in terms of his inability to speak.

582
00:43:08,525 --> 00:43:17,199
But what is different here; is that even though, he was unable to speak; he never stopped calling the people to making;

583
00:43:17,232 --> 00:43:18,589
الأمر بالمعروف والنهي عن المنكر

584
00:43:19,112 --> 00:43:25,842
Zakariyya(زَكَرِيا); even though, he was unable to speak for those three days; he did not discontinue in joining good and forbidding evil.

585
00:43:26,255 --> 00:43:27,215
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

586
00:43:27,235 --> 00:43:31,800
فَخَرَجَ عَلَىٰ قَوْمِهِۦ مِنَ ٱلْمِحْرَابِ فَأَوْحَىٰٓ إِلَيْهِمْ أَن سَبِّحُواْ بُكْرَةً وَعَشِيًّا۝

587
00:43:32,087 --> 00:43:43,123
Then, he came out to his people from his place of worship, and he told them by signs, to glorify Allah in the morning and in the afternoons.

588
00:43:43,610 --> 00:43:53,291
So even though, he was unable to speak; he still was giving the people orders using signs, that they should make the Dhikr(ذكر) to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

589
00:43:53,705 --> 00:44:01,194
And this is an indication to us that we are in our full physical abilities, and we are withholding;

590
00:44:01,867 --> 00:44:03,307
أمر بالمعروف والنهي عن المنكر

591
00:44:03,347 --> 00:44:07,826
We are withholding Da'wah(دعوة); even though, we are fully capable of doing it.

592
00:44:08,293 --> 00:44:19,538
Sayidina Zakariyyahعليه السلام was not capable of speaking for three days, that did not deter him from fulfilling his duties of Da'wah(دعوة) to his people.

593
00:44:20,442 --> 00:44:26,020
And this shows you the amazing devotion, that the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى had.

594
00:44:26,800 --> 00:44:33,112
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى in the next three Ayaat(آيات); actually four; talks about Sayidina Yahya(سيدنا يحيى).

595
00:44:33,392 --> 00:44:34,232
Allah says;

596
00:44:34,612 --> 00:44:36,772
يَا يَحْيَىٰ خُذِ الْكِتَابَ بِقُوَّةٍ ۖ

597
00:44:37,699 --> 00:44:42,898
Allah says; Oh Yahya(يحيى)! Hold fast the scripture.

598
00:44:43,365 --> 00:44:44,085
خُذِ الْكِتَابَ

599
00:44:44,158 --> 00:44:45,977
Kitab(كتاب) is a scripture; At-Torah(التّوراة).

600
00:44:46,990 --> 00:44:48,110
بِقُوَّةٍ ۖ

601
00:44:48,870 --> 00:44:50,749
What does this word mean; Quwwah(قُوَّة)?

602
00:44:51,109 --> 00:44:52,855
Here it says; hold fast.

603
00:44:53,242 --> 00:44:54,682
But what is the meaning of the word Quwwah(قُوَّة)?

604
00:44:55,735 --> 00:44:57,684
Quwwah(قُوَّة) is power and strength.

605
00:44:59,344 --> 00:45:00,551
That's the meaning of Quwwah(قُوَّة).

606
00:45:01,111 --> 00:45:07,990
What this means is that; you hold fast to all of the commands of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, and you don't let go of them.

607
00:45:09,283 --> 00:45:13,345
So you never give up and you never buckle down.

608
00:45:14,805 --> 00:45:18,607
You're always holding fast, holding strong to the commands of Allah.

609
00:45:19,827 --> 00:45:23,688
Yahya عليه السلام; because we need to understand the position of Yahya(يحيى).

610
00:45:24,381 --> 00:45:31,904
Yahya عليه السلام is young and he is going to be the Nabi(نَبِي) of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

611
00:45:32,284 --> 00:45:36,173
Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) who, went corrupt, and went astray.

612
00:45:36,873 --> 00:45:42,392
And this young man will be responsible for this ummah(امة); for this nation.

613
00:45:43,032 --> 00:45:47,372
Therefore; he must have that strength and confidence and power.

614
00:45:48,159 --> 00:45:50,981
Otherwise, he would not be able to function.

615
00:45:51,481 --> 00:45:58,609
And he would be swept away by the ocean of corruption that was existing in the time.

616
00:45:59,975 --> 00:46:06,278
Sayidina Yahyaعليه السلام never gave up this order of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى,

617
00:46:06,644 --> 00:46:11,443
and the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; they never give up the orders of Allah; they fulfill them.

618
00:46:12,083 --> 00:46:14,883
So, Sayidina Yahya(سيدنا يحيى) received this order from Allah.

619
00:46:15,650 --> 00:46:18,975
And that is that you should hold fast and strong to the religion.

620
00:46:19,508 --> 00:46:24,718
So Sayidina Yahyaعليه السلام held strong to the religion of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى,

621
00:46:24,931 --> 00:46:29,211
and he ended up giving his life for the religion of Allah, and he died as As-Shaheed(الشَّهِيد).

622
00:46:29,971 --> 00:46:36,197
Because, of holding strong to the religion; Sayidina Yahyaعليه السلام was assassinated.

623
00:46:37,170 --> 00:46:39,628
That was the end of the life of Sayidina Yahya(سيدنا يحيى).

624
00:46:39,855 --> 00:46:43,708
It was a life of struggle; a life of striving; a difficult life.

625
00:46:44,148 --> 00:46:51,230
But Sayidina Yahya(سيدنا يحيى) was able to hold throughout that period with patience, until he faced Allahسُبحانه وتعالى as As-Shaheed(الشَّهِيد).

626
00:46:51,644 --> 00:47:00,427
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; now even though; Allah Has given him this very strong responsibility, or very heavy responsibility,

627
00:47:00,678 --> 00:47:05,003
but Allahسُبحانه وتعالى gave him the tools and the ability to fulfill it.

628
00:47:05,283 --> 00:47:06,223
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

629
00:47:06,243 --> 00:47:07,716
وَآتَيْنَاهُ الْحُكْمَ صَبِيًّا۝

630
00:47:08,445 --> 00:47:14,143
We Have given him the judgment, and the understanding, and the wisdom; when he was young.

631
00:47:14,530 --> 00:47:17,850
Because Allahسُبحانه وتعالى does not overburden a person.

632
00:47:18,550 --> 00:47:21,199
Allah will not ask you to do something, you're un capable of doing.

633
00:47:21,726 --> 00:47:26,269
Since, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has put a very heavy responsibility on Sayidina Yahya(سيدنا يحيى).

634
00:47:26,415 --> 00:47:33,182
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى also equipped Sayidina Yahya(سيدنا يحيى) with the tools to carry on with that responsibility and that is;

635
00:47:33,216 --> 00:47:34,742
الْحُكْمَ صَبِيًّا

636
00:47:34,842 --> 00:47:38,893
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Has given him this understanding very, very early on.

637
00:47:39,120 --> 00:47:42,929
And the Mufassireen(مفسرين) mentions some things, for example;

638
00:47:43,515 --> 00:47:49,935
they say that Yahya(يحيى) was a kid, was a child and the children came to him and said;

639
00:47:50,228 --> 00:47:52,341
Let's go and play; very young child.

640
00:47:52,555 --> 00:47:54,147
So Sayidina Yahyaعليه السلام said;

641
00:47:54,367 --> 00:47:55,667
ما لله بخلقنا

642
00:47:55,967 --> 00:47:57,287
We were not created to play.

643
00:47:57,540 --> 00:48:00,566
So he was serious from his childhood.

644
00:48:01,606 --> 00:48:02,979
وَحَنَانًا مِّن لَّدُنَّا

645
00:48:03,012 --> 00:48:04,146
He was sympathetic.

646
00:48:05,132 --> 00:48:11,464
Don't understand that strength means; I mean; because sometimes, we misinterpret words.

647
00:48:11,791 --> 00:48:17,480
Don't think that strength means; being extreme, or being rude, or being rough.

648
00:48:17,513 --> 00:48:19,187
That's not the meaning of the word strong.

649
00:48:20,160 --> 00:48:22,024
Rasool Allah ﷺ was the strongest.

650
00:48:23,704 --> 00:48:25,364
But he was still the most merciful.

651
00:48:25,851 --> 00:48:27,214
بِالْمُؤْمِنِينَ رَءُوفٌ رَّحِيمٌ۝

652
00:48:27,707 --> 00:48:30,141
With the believers; merciful and compassionate.

653
00:48:30,914 --> 00:48:39,919
Because sometimes, we think that strong means that, you have a very rough heart, insensitive, have no sympathy, no mercy that's not what is meant by strength.

654
00:48:40,245 --> 00:48:45,063
What is meant by strength is; that you're holding to the commands of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى completely.

655
00:48:47,090 --> 00:48:55,035
All of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allah was sympathetic, but Sayidina Yahya(سيدنا يحيى); that was a strong attribute of him.

656
00:48:55,375 --> 00:48:58,061
Some of the Mufassireen(مفسرين) say; it means; sympathetic towards his parents.

657
00:48:58,281 --> 00:49:01,061
Some of them say; its general; he was sympathetic towards all people.

658
00:49:01,934 --> 00:49:02,553
وَزَكَوٰةً ۖ

659
00:49:02,593 --> 00:49:03,733
And he was pure.

660
00:49:03,993 --> 00:49:04,646
وَكَانَ تَقِيًّا۝

661
00:49:04,686 --> 00:49:06,593
And he was righteous.

662
00:49:06,706 --> 00:49:09,669
وَبَرًّا بِوَالِدَيْهِ وَلَمْ يَكُن جَبَّارًا عَصِيًّا۝

663
00:49:09,842 --> 00:49:15,109
And dutiful towards his parents, and he was neither arrogant nor disobedient.

664
00:49:15,835 --> 00:49:20,297
Security and peace is important for us in our life.

665
00:49:21,677 --> 00:49:27,133
The most difficult phases are the transition phases that we go through.

666
00:49:27,507 --> 00:49:31,479
And we go through three transition phases.

667
00:49:31,906 --> 00:49:43,609
When we're in the wombs of our mothers; we spend nine months in the comfort and warmth of the mother's body.

668
00:49:45,049 --> 00:49:48,575
It's very cozy and small room warm.

669
00:49:49,281 --> 00:49:54,111
So the child is comfortable; you never hear the child crying in the womb of the mother.

670
00:49:55,444 --> 00:50:03,343
When the child is delivered; the child is going through a completely different stage of their life.

671
00:50:04,137 --> 00:50:09,359
They're going from the nine months stage in the womb to a completely different world.

672
00:50:09,892 --> 00:50:14,381
So the warmth and small, coziness of the womb of the mother disappears.

673
00:50:14,415 --> 00:50:18,755
Suddenly, you come in a completely open space.

674
00:50:19,041 --> 00:50:21,110
So the first reaction of the child is what?

675
00:50:21,577 --> 00:50:22,184
Cry.

676
00:50:23,150 --> 00:50:24,577
It's a difficult transition.

677
00:50:25,144 --> 00:50:27,866
That phase of transition is difficult.

678
00:50:28,560 --> 00:50:30,900
Because you're going to an entirely different stage.

679
00:50:31,100 --> 00:50:33,213
You're going to the unexpected and the unknown.

680
00:50:34,473 --> 00:50:37,563
And then; we live in this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) and we get used to it.

681
00:50:37,743 --> 00:50:40,689
Unfortunately, some of us get too much attached to it.

682
00:50:41,689 --> 00:50:47,161
We spent here some time and then it's time for us to move to the next stage.

683
00:50:47,755 --> 00:50:52,324
So we go through another transition phase, and that is; death.

684
00:50:53,630 --> 00:50:54,750
ان سكرات الموت

685
00:50:54,950 --> 00:51:01,937
The last moments, you find that the person is going through consciousness and unconsciousness, and that alternates.

686
00:51:02,464 --> 00:51:06,682
That person is actually going back and forth, in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا); in and out.

687
00:51:07,715 --> 00:51:14,214
And that transition phase, is slowly taking the person out of the realm of this world.

688
00:51:14,327 --> 00:51:18,951
Slowly, slowly, he's leaving this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) and the person is aware that he's leaving.

689
00:51:19,049 --> 00:51:24,562
And that's much much more difficult than the transition phase that we talked about before.

690
00:51:25,182 --> 00:51:34,081
Because you spent a long time in this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا), and now you're leaving to a completely unknown world and that is, Al-Barzakh(البرزخ); the grave.

691
00:51:34,954 --> 00:51:37,047
And those are very difficult moments.

692
00:51:37,273 --> 00:51:40,720
And Rasool Allah ﷺ has spoken them in the Ahadith(احاديث) and the Ayaat(آيات) of Qur'an;

693
00:51:40,740 --> 00:51:43,722
وَجَاءَتْ سَكْرَةُ الْمَوْتِ بِالْحَقِّ ۖ ذَٰلِكَ مَا كُنتَ مِنْهُ تَحِيدُ۝

694
00:51:43,929 --> 00:51:48,196
Now the moments of death have approached you; that is what you're trying to run away from.

695
00:51:48,876 --> 00:51:50,576
You can't run away from it now; you're facing it.

696
00:51:50,803 --> 00:51:53,123
And here you are; you're going to cross the line.

697
00:51:53,203 --> 00:51:55,102
And as soon as you cross it; there's no way back.

698
00:51:56,568 --> 00:52:03,284
That's another very critical and difficult phase of the human being.

699
00:52:04,804 --> 00:52:08,528
And then you are living in your graves; you have awareness.

700
00:52:09,401 --> 00:52:12,185
Even though, your body can't move, but you're still conscious.

701
00:52:12,945 --> 00:52:17,165
And now it's time for you to go through the third transition phase.

702
00:52:17,591 --> 00:52:20,600
And that is; the resurrection and this is the worse.

703
00:52:21,113 --> 00:52:29,646
Because now; you suddenly have a grave that has popped open; you crawl out of that grave.

704
00:52:30,646 --> 00:52:33,385
And you come and see an entirely different world.

705
00:52:33,725 --> 00:52:35,685
The sky above your head is cracking.

706
00:52:36,025 --> 00:52:37,992
The stars are falling down.

707
00:52:38,085 --> 00:52:39,870
The moon knocked out of his orbit.

708
00:52:40,137 --> 00:52:41,737
The sun right over your head.

709
00:52:42,210 --> 00:52:45,282
Mountains are exploding and turning into dirt.

710
00:52:45,842 --> 00:52:48,322
The oceans are catching fire and burning.

711
00:52:48,742 --> 00:52:50,887
There's an earthquake and it's cracking open.

712
00:52:51,134 --> 00:52:53,754
And you see people running around you as if they're drunk.

713
00:52:54,127 --> 00:52:58,603
So that is the worst; that is the worst of the three transition stages.

714
00:52:59,216 --> 00:53:03,723
And this is when we need security and peace most.

715
00:53:04,290 --> 00:53:06,041
Because these are the most difficult moments.

716
00:53:06,081 --> 00:53:12,876
When you read the description of what happens in Al-Ba'th(اَلْبَعَثْ); it is something unbelievable.

717
00:53:13,050 --> 00:53:14,530
If we are able to comprehend it.

718
00:53:15,663 --> 00:53:19,595
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has give Sayidina Yahya(سيدنا يحيى) very, very interesting blessing.

719
00:53:20,148 --> 00:53:21,715
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

720
00:53:21,975 --> 00:53:29,454
وَسَلَامٌ عَلَيْهِ يَوْمَ وُلِدَ وَيَوْمَ يَمُوتُ وَيَوْمَ يُبْعَثُ حَيًّا۝

721
00:53:30,121 --> 00:53:41,660
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; And peace be on him; the day he was born; and the day he dies; and the day he will be raised up again.

722
00:53:43,487 --> 00:53:52,282
See in these three difficult moments; these critical moments; when you are in great need, in dire need of peace;

723
00:53:52,709 --> 00:53:55,038
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given that peace to Sayidina Yahya(سيدنا يحيى).

724
00:53:56,132 --> 00:53:58,691
Allah has given him peace when he was born; the day he was born.

725
00:53:58,965 --> 00:54:02,453
And Allah gave him peace; the day he died.

726
00:54:02,666 --> 00:54:06,735
And Allah Will give him peace the day he will be resurrected again.

727
00:54:06,908 --> 00:54:10,715
We ask Allahسُبحانه وتعالى to give us peace.

728
00:54:11,641 --> 00:54:15,684
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

